# The July-2026 counterexample to the Jacobian conjecture (Alpoege/Fable),
# verified over Z. Companion to the tutorial at
# https://zelph.org/math/tutorial-jacobian/
#
#   .import examples/math/jacobian
#   _M jdet _P              # answers (neg zint &512)
#
# The original map F : C^3 -> C^3 has constant Jacobian determinant -2 yet
# sends three distinct points to one image, refuting the conjecture for
# n >= 3. Substituting x=a, y=b/2, z=c/4 and clearing denominators gives
# G = (32*F1, 16*F2, 4*F3) with INTEGER coefficients, so the whole
# verification stays inside the natural/zint substrate -- no fractions.
# By the chain rule det J_G = 2048*(-2)/8 = -512, and conversely
# det J_G == -512 as a polynomial identity implies det J_F == -2.
#
# This file proves the determinant half. The collision half is three
# ground evaluations; see the tutorial, or test_jacobian.cpp, which builds
# both halves from ONE Janet constructor parameterized over its leaves.

# The deduction echo of a workload this size is thousands of lines and
# says nothing the final answer does not. Comment out to watch it.
.deductions off

.import math

<a b c> ~ polyring

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rules J1-J9 -- Request the nine partial derivatives. A 3x3 Jacobian is
# stated as (<F G H> jac3 <X Y Z>): rows are components, columns are
# variables. Lists rather than three objects on one fact, because a fact
# carries a SET of objects and the order of rows and columns matters.
# Matching three cells deep is ordinary deep unification.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
((F cons (G cons (H cons nil))) jac3 (X cons (Y cons (Z cons nil)))) => (F diffby X)
((F cons (G cons (H cons nil))) jac3 (X cons (Y cons (Z cons nil)))) => (F diffby Y)
((F cons (G cons (H cons nil))) jac3 (X cons (Y cons (Z cons nil)))) => (F diffby Z)
((F cons (G cons (H cons nil))) jac3 (X cons (Y cons (Z cons nil)))) => (G diffby X)
((F cons (G cons (H cons nil))) jac3 (X cons (Y cons (Z cons nil)))) => (G diffby Y)
((F cons (G cons (H cons nil))) jac3 (X cons (Y cons (Z cons nil)))) => (G diffby Z)
((F cons (G cons (H cons nil))) jac3 (X cons (Y cons (Z cons nil)))) => (H diffby X)
((F cons (G cons (H cons nil))) jac3 (X cons (Y cons (Z cons nil)))) => (H diffby Y)
((F cons (G cons (H cons nil))) jac3 (X cons (Y cons (Z cons nil)))) => (H diffby Z)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rule JD -- Assemble: the first-row cofactor expansion,
#   det = D11*(D22*D33 - D23*D32)
#       - D12*(D21*D33 - D23*D31)
#       + D13*(D21*D32 - D22*D31)
# written over the nine simplified derivative results. diff exposes each
# under =, so they are ordinary conditions.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
((F cons (G cons (H cons nil))) jac3 (X cons (Y cons (Z cons nil))),
 (F diffby X) = _P, (F diffby Y) = _Q, (F diffby Z) = _R,
 (G diffby X) = _S, (G diffby Y) = _T, (G diffby Z) = _U,
 (H diffby X) = _V, (H diffby Y) = _W, (H diffby Z) = _N)
=> (((F cons (G cons (H cons nil))) jac3 (X cons (Y cons (Z cons nil)))) detis
    (((_P * ((_T * _N) - (_U * _W)))
      - (_Q * ((_S * _N) - (_U * _V))))
      + (_R * ((_S * _W) - (_T * _V)))))

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rules JC -- Connect: compile the assembled determinant to its polynomial
# normal form. A CONSTANT result is the whole point -- it is the statement
# that every non-constant term cancelled, as an identity rather than at
# sample points.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(M detis D) => (D topoly D)
(M detis D, (D topoly D) = P) => (M jdet P)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The map G, one component per island. Must stay on one line: the REPL
# reads statements line by line.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
< $( (2+a*b)^3*c + 2*b^2*(2+a*b)*(8+3*a*b) ) $( 8*b + 3*a*(2+a*b)^2*c + 6*a*b^2*(8+3*a*b) ) $( 8*a - (6*a^2*b + a^3*c) ) > jac3 <a b c>

.run
